# Example only. Do not install this as /etc/environment.d/ or a global
# systemd default. Ubuntu 24.04's glibc / THP / pymalloc defaults are
# faster for mixed workloads than the knobs below (see
# ubuntu24/benchmarks/MEMORY.md).
#
# Copy a *single* line into one service unit after measuring that service.

# Memory-tight, mostly-idle daemon that is not allocator-bound:
# GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.arena_max=2

# Never set these globally:
# GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.arena_max=1
# GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.tcache_count=0
# PYTHONMALLOC=malloc
